man what a click bait title right why is  elden ring dying which is definitely a  bold claim coming from a guy whose  channel is almost completely based on  elden ring and uncovering the incredibly  complicated story behind it but if we  look at the steam charts and the google  trends for eldon rings player base and  overall interest in the game it's  definitely started to take a huge dive  so today we're going to talk about why  that's the case because in my opinion it  isn't that the game is actually dying we  are all just probably a bit burnt out  from the game we all just kind of beat  the game right or most of us did anyway  see i play elden ring for multiple hours  every single day because it's my job now  i'm trying to learn everything that  there is about this game and because of  its massive size and complicated story  that's a giant endeavor that requires me  to play it every single day but for me  that's a dream job so i definitely don't  mind it i absolutely love it but for the  rest of the player base who i'm assuming  can't play video games every day all day  because they have school or work or  other life responsibilities don't really  want to play elden ring after they've  beat it that one time now this is sort  of strange because these players have  probably booted up other online  multiplayer games like valorant call of  duty apex legends fortnite whatever it  may be and they play it every day at  least for a little while but with eldon  ring they may not do that and why is  that because elden ring is mainly a  single player experience that during our  first or second playthrough of the game  might possibly be the best experience in  all of gaming that first playthrough is  just filled with incredible moments that  i'm going to remember for the rest of my  life and even during my second  playthrough i was finding out new things  about the game every single time i  played it because there's just so much  to discover there's so much content to  consume that it's somewhat overwhelming  at times that could be a part of another  issue that i'll talk about in a bit but  for now i believe the main issue is that  you aren't going to get that amazing  first playthrough experience ever again  once you sort of know where every boss  is where every item location is every  secret discovery you may find that  feeling of discovery and exploration  fade away which is what open world games  are for they are meant for you to  explore a giant open world and discover  for yourself all of the amazing things  that there are to find but once you've  found everything which mind you takes  hundreds of hours in the world of elden  ring to fully complete then there really  isn't much more to do after that once  you've played all of the content that  there is to offer and once you're out of  content you're going to move on to the  next thing more likely than not but why  isn't this the case with the multiplayer  games that i mentioned earlier because  the experience of competing against  other players is most of the time a  completely different experience every  time you enter a match there are  different players maps weapons to use  things like that that make the  experience different every time you play  it whereas with elden ring the field of  play doesn't really change ever once  you've discovered those areas and beaten  those bosses you know what to expect  they even use the same movements against  you which is fun to perfect and beat  bosses without having much trouble  eventually once you get good enough  that's why there's such a big interest  in modded playthroughs or challenge runs  of souls games it really mixes up the  formula to make the game or the  challenge different and interesting from  what we are used to and obviously in  elden ring you can make different builds  to give yourself a slightly different  experience but when i'm talking about  the field of play meaning the map and  the bosses and things to discover you're  only gonna get that really one or two  times or one or two playthroughs and you  might be asking but jake eldon ring does  have multiplayer and you'd be right  there is a ton of potential for elden  ring in regards to pvp there's so many  different build types weapons spells  buffs incantations that can make every  invasion or duel a truly different  experience every time not to mention the  endless amount of locations where you  can fight and duel and just completely  change the setting of that unfortunately  from my understanding the pvp community  for elden ring is in a pretty tough spot  right now now i'm not a pvp player  myself but i've been paying attention to  those who are and what they think  because i understand the major  importance of multiplayer in regards to  a game's longevity and continued  interest over time especially with a  game that i love to death like elden  ring and from what i've heard there's  some serious issues with certain weapons  in pvp that are just completely  unbalanced obviously when a weapon or a  spell or whatever it is is overpowered  and gives the player the best chance at  success of beating their opponent they  are going to use that weapon 9 times out  of 10. this is the case with almost  every multiplayer game out there i used  to play a lot of warzone and most of the  time there would be a particular meta  where the entire player base only used  one type of gun because it was seen as  the best gun to use and to win the game  most of the time the developers would  see that weapons usage was much higher  than other weapons and they just nerfed  that weapon into the ground so it  wouldn't be used as much now i  definitely don't think this is the best  way to handle it because we all remember  what happened to horfrost stomp it was  used by quite literally everybody  because it was so powerful and then they  nerfed it into nothingness and it isn't  even used in pve anymore there is a  needed balance that i'm sure is  extremely difficult to hit in all of  these games especially with elden ring  when there are so many different weapons  and abilities that need to somehow be  balanced together there's also the issue  of certain players not fully  understanding how pvp works in from  software games in elden ring apparently  there's a stigma against invasions where  a player can invade another player's  world during their playthrough to try  and kill them and this has been an  aspect and a feature of from software's  game design for forever at this point  invasions are not a new thing however  with elden rings worldwide success there  are a lot of new players who quite  frankly don't understand how pvp works  and just see invasions as a way to annoy  or ruin a player's playthrough by  randomly entering their world and just  killing them yeah it's the invader's  goal to invade your world and kill you  but it isn't to completely ruin your  playthrough if you die all you lose is a  slight bit of progression from the last  sight of grace and the runes that you  can more than likely get back with no  problem at all it's an exciting aspect  of the game to not know when you're  going to be invaded or where you will be  invaded it keeps the player on their  toes at all times and is obviously very  enjoyable for the invader to pull off a  kill since they get certain rewards for  successfully killing the host of that  world they invaded unfortunately the new  player base has sort of stigmatized  invasions as nothing more than pure  annoyance and it has gotten to the point  where everyone has just turned their  games offline and don't even bother with  the online aspects of the game doing  this reduces the amount of players  co-opting with their friends and then in  turn reduces the amount of invadable  worlds for the players who do want to  participate in the pvp eventually that  offline player will beat everything in  the game and they will just stop playing  the game all together same goes to the  pvper who will likely stop playing the  game because they can never find a world  to invade and participate in the  multiplayer both sides of the spectrum  people who like and don't like pvp are  sort of shooting themselves in the foot  essentially now i believe all of this  will be addressed soon because why else  would from software design these  coliseums that we cannot currently enter  that are spread all over the world if  they weren't going to be used for either  pve boss fights and maybe a boss rush  mod or a perfect area for pvp from  software definitely needs to get on this  issue if they do want their player base  to go back up they are more than likely  working on the first dlc for elden ring  right now which i'm sure will revitalize  the player base to come back and get  that next new experience like we were  talking about earlier again this is a  big reason multiplayer games hold their  player bases for long periods of time  they are constantly pushing out updates  that can keep their player base playing  and interested new content will always  bring players back with elden ring the  game was and is so incredibly good that  all of those players that are currently  burnt out on the game will likely come  back as soon as new content is released  you could even argue that players will  be even more excited for new elden ring  content compared to other games because  while they don't release new content all  that often and again the game is so good  on its own already that there isn't any  type of stain on the game for it not  releasing new updates or new content  more often we got such a high quality  experience with the main release of  elden ring then i am more than happy to  wait for new updates to release and new  content to come out if it matches that  high quality experience there was a  massive amount of content that we  consumed at launch but four months is  more than enough time for most players  to have beaten most stuff in the game  and have just moved on to something else  another small thing i'd like to bring up  that may only be a case for myself and  if you feel the same way let me know but  i don't like making new characters in  elden ring i like having my first  character that i started out with in my  first playthrough and getting that  character as strong as possible i enjoy  going from struggling in my first  playthrough to completely destroying  bosses in new game plus it makes me feel  like my character and i have gone  through all of this adversity together  and have overcome it together as well as  soon as i make a new character i feel  like i abandoned my previous character  it's kind of a weird feeling it's also  not super inviting to go from that  overpowered state that you work so hard  to achieve back down to where it all  started in this super weak state the  sheer size and scope of doing all of  that again with a completely new  character is overwhelming and somewhat  daunting of a task that i guarantee a  lot of players will just pass on now  this video may really seem like i'm  talking negatively about the game but i  really don't think eldon ring is dying  whatsoever the player base might be  lower but like i said all of those  players are going to come back as soon  as new content releases it's clearly  been a major success and i'm happy to  see from software finally get the  mainstream exposure i've always thought  their games deserved but when something  goes mainstream there's definitely going  to be side effects like we talked about  elden ring is one of the best games i've  ever played is it my favorite souls game  my opinion has kind of changed on that  the more i've played the game it's just  a totally different experience from  let's say bloodborne to elden ring they  are two totally different things that i  think stack up right next to each other  in quality of what the game is designed  for and i think that's because along  with a major part of the player base is  that we've all displayed everything that  there is to offer with elden ring and  we're all just a bit burnt out for now  but what do you guys think let me know  down in the comments and also let me  know if you'd like to see more  commentary videos like this i used to do  these kinds of videos all the time on a  previous channel i love talking and  discussing all things gaming with my  community doesn't have to be just souls  games so hopefully you would like that  as well let me know down below have a  great rest of your day and i will see  you all in the next one take care
 

